<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  REACTION_MECHANISM_GENERALISE_1 step 1 / GREENTIDE_WASP_SWARM_1. The mental
  state a reaction source's spawned pawns (skerrels, and any future spawn
  response wired the same way) start in: hostile to the one pawn that
  disturbed the source, never a map-wide manhunter flip, and self-ending once
  that pawn is far enough from the disturbance — see
  RM_MentalState_ScopedAggression's own header for why (it is this assembly's
  RM_MentalState_ParentalEnrage shape, generalised from "anchored on a pawn"
  to "anchored on a cell").

  RM tier: names no species. RM_ReactionResponseRule_SpawnPawns.startMentalState
  points at this def from a content mod's own CompProperties_ReactionSource XML;
  nothing here knows what a skerrel is.

  Same reasoning as RM_ParentalEnrage_MentalStates.xml for shape and timing:
  stateClass derives from vanilla MentalState_Manhunter so
  ThinkNode_ConditionalMentalStateClass's instance check (not a def-identity
  check) routes it through JobGiver_Manhunter's whole chase-and-melee behaviour
  with no think-tree patch (MEASURED 2026-09-20, same engine read). No
  ParentName, for the same reason: minTicksBeforeRecovery/recoveryMtbDays both
  need overriding to be SHORT anyway. No beginLetter: a boiling gall is its own
  notification, and "no warning" reads the same way here as it does for the
  guardian rage.

  Timing kept SHORTER than RM_ParentalEnrage's own 600/0.05: a wasp is meant to
  be outrun in a handful of seconds once its target backs off, not to hold a
  grudge for a quarter hour. RM_MentalState_ScopedAggression's own disengage
  check (distance from the disturbance) ends it long before either floor is
  reached in the ordinary case; these are the backstop for a target that never
  leaves range.
-->
<Defs>

  <MentalStateDef>
    <defName>RM_SwarmAggression</defName>
    <label>swarming</label>
    <stateClass>RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_MentalState_ScopedAggression</stateClass>
    <category>Aggro</category>
    <baseInspectLine>Swarming the disturbance</baseInspectLine>
    <recoveryMessage>{0} has stopped swarming.</recoveryMessage>
    <nameColor>(0.85,0.7,0.15)</nameColor>
    <minTicksBeforeRecovery>60</minTicksBeforeRecovery>
    <recoveryMtbDays>0.2</recoveryMtbDays>
    <stopsJobs>true</stopsJobs>
    <recoverFromDowned>true</recoverFromDowned>
    <recoverFromSleep>true</recoverFromSleep>
    <inCaravanCanDo>false</inCaravanCanDo>
  </MentalStateDef>

</Defs>
